; Draw the entities of the room and test them against Willy
;
; Walks the entity buffer (#R$8100, 8 bytes per entity, an entry whose byte +0 is $FF ends the list) and draws
; every entity into the pixel buffer at $6000 and the attribute buffer at $5C00, on top of the room and of Willy,
; who #R$95C8 has already drawn. The entity type is bits 0-2 of byte +0: 0 is skipped, 3 is the rope (#R$92A4),
; 4 the arrow (#R$9237), anything else (1 and 2; 5-7 would be treated the same) a sprite guardian (#R$91D6). A
; collision jumps to #R$90B7 (KillWilly), which abandons the frame update, so the entities after the one that hit
; Willy are not drawn in that pass. Moving the entities is #R$90C0, except for the arrow, which moves here.
; .
; Guardian (types 1 and 2): +0 type and animation bits, +1 bits 0-2 ink, bit 3 bright, bits 5-7 frame mask,
; +2 bits 0-4 column of the left cell, bits 5-7 frame offset, +3 Y index (twice the pixel row, as in #R$8200),
; +5 sprite page. The sprite address is page * 256 + F with F = ((+0 AND +1) OR +2) AND $E0, so the frame number
; is bits 5-7 (the mask in +1 decides how much of the animation bits of +0 selects the frame, the bits of +2 are
; or-ed in). First the attributes: the 2 x 2 cells under the sprite (2 x 3 when the Y index is not a multiple of
; 16) get the ink and bright bits of +1, keeping the paper of the background and clearing flash. Then
; #R$9456 draws the sprite into the $6000 buffer with the collision test (C = 1): any lit pixel already there
; (Willy, but also the room tiles) kills Willy (F83).
; .
; Arrow (type 4, #R$9237): +0 bit 7 direction, +2 Y index of its centre row (bit 7 = lower half of the room), +4 X
; column (moves one column per pass), +5 scratch (collision mask), +6 pixel pattern of the fins. See F84, F85,
; F86: it is drawn only while X is 0-31, as one cell wide: the fin pattern above and below a solid centre row,
; in white ink; when X reaches $2C (left) or $F4 (right) the pass makes a rising chirp instead (128 speaker
; toggles, about 32 ms). It kills Willy when its attribute cell has ink 7 and the centre row byte is not empty.
; Quirk (F92): the arrow of The Attic has the odd Y index $D5, so the row table is read half a word off and its
; pixels go to $9F6A+X and $A06A+X (inside #R$A000), its attributes to $5D6A+X.
; .
; Rope (type 3, #R$92A4): +1 swing position (moved by #R$90C0), +2 column of the top, +3 scratch (current column),
; +4 length in segments ($20 gives 33 points), +5 scratch (pixel mask, starts at $80). The rope also uses the
; entry after it: its byte +1 is the segment counter (the rope's byte +9) and bit 0 of its byte +3 the held flag
; (the rope's byte +11), so a rope is followed by an arrow or by the $FF end marker (F90). The rope is a chain of
; one-pixel points starting at pixel row 0 of the room; the next point is found from #R$8300 with the index
; segment + swing distance: the second half gives the rows down (row table bytes, 2 per pixel row), the first half
; the pixels sideways (left when bit 7 of +1 is set, else right). Points are ORed into the buffer, in the ink of
; the background.
; .
; Willy and the rope use #R$85D6: 0 = Willy holds no rope; 1-$20 = number of the rope segment he holds; $F0-$FF =
; he has just let go (counts up by 1 per rope pass, so for 16 passes he cannot grab again). While it is 0, any lit
; pixel of the buffer under a rope point grabs the rope there (Willy, drawn earlier, is the normal case; a room
; tile or another entity would do it too, F87). While held, every pass puts Willy on the rope: his Y index
; (#R$85CF) is the Y index of the point minus $10 (the rope passes through the middle of the sprite), his column
; and frame (#R$85D3, #R$85D2) are taken from the pixel mask of the point (mask $80 or $40: frame 2, $20 or $10:
; frame 3, both with the column one to the left; $08 or $04: frame 0, $02 or $01: frame 1, in the point's own
; column), and #R$8E9C recomputes his attribute address. At the end of the rope (F88, F89): during the release countdown
; $85D6 is counted up and the held flag cleared; otherwise, if the rope is held and Willy walks (bit 1 of #R$85D0),
; $85D6 goes down one segment (higher up) or up one segment (lower down): +1 when his facing (bit 0 of #R$85D0,
; 1 = left) differs from the swing direction bit (bit 7 of +0), else -1. In a room whose up exit (#R$80EB) is the
; room itself he cannot go above segment $0C. Past the last segment he is let go: #R$85D6 := $F0, his Y index is
; rounded down to a multiple of 8 and the jump/fall state #R$85D1 is cleared. Quirk (F91): a lit pixel under
; point 0 sets the held flag and moves Willy to the top of the rope without setting $85D6.
; .
; Hardware: writes the $6000 pixel buffer and the $5C00 attribute buffer; the arrow chirp toggles the speaker and
; border bits of port $FE in a busy-wait loop.
@label=DrawEntities
c$91BE LD IX,$8100     ;
@label=DrawEntities_Loop
*$91C2 LD A,(IX+$00)   ;
@isub=CP ENTITY_END
 $91C5 CP $FF          ;
 $91C7 RET Z           ;
@isub=AND ENTITY_TYPE_MASK
 $91C8 AND $07         ;
 $91CA JP Z,$93B3      ; empty
@isub=CP ENTITY_ROPE
 $91CD CP $03          ;
 $91CF JP Z,$92A4      ;
@isub=CP ENTITY_ARROW
 $91D2 CP $04          ;
 $91D4 JR Z,$9237      ;
@label=DrawEntities_Guardian
@isub=LD E,(IX+ENT_Y)
 $91D6 LD E,(IX+$03)   ; guardian: E = Y index
@isub=LD D,RowAddressTable>>8
 $91D9 LD D,$82        ;
 $91DB LD A,(DE)       ; low byte of the row address in the buffer
 $91DC LD L,A          ;
@isub=LD A,(IX+ENT_COLUMN)
 $91DD LD A,(IX+$02)   ; plus the column
@isub=AND COLUMN_MASK
 $91E0 AND $1F         ;
 $91E2 ADD A,L         ;
 $91E3 LD L,A          ;
 $91E4 LD A,E          ; Y index bit 7: upper or lower half of the room
 $91E5 RLCA            ;
 $91E6 AND $01         ;
@isub=OR SCREEN_ATTRS_BUF>>8
 $91E8 OR $5C          ;
 $91EA LD H,A          ; HL = attribute buffer address of the top-left cell
@isub=LD DE,SCREEN_COLS-1
 $91EB LD DE,$001F     ; to the next row of cells, one column left
 $91EE LD A,(IX+$01)   ;
@isub=AND ENTITY_ATTR_MASK
 $91F1 AND $0F         ; ink and bright
@isub=ADD A,WHITE*PAPER
 $91F3 ADD A,$38       ; bright becomes bit 6, the paper bits are cleared by the next AND
@isub=AND BRIGHT+INK_MASK
 $91F5 AND $47         ;
 $91F7 LD C,A          ; C = attribute without paper
 $91F8 LD A,(HL)       ;
@isub=AND PAPER_MASK
 $91F9 AND $38         ; keep the paper of the background
 $91FB XOR C           ;
 $91FC LD C,A          ;
 $91FD LD (HL),C       ;
 $91FE INC HL          ;
 $91FF LD (HL),C       ;
 $9200 ADD HL,DE       ;
 $9201 LD (HL),C       ;
 $9202 INC HL          ;
 $9203 LD (HL),C       ;
@isub=LD A,(IX+ENT_Y)
 $9204 LD A,(IX+$03)   ; Y index in the lower bits
@isub=AND Y_BETWEEN_MASK
 $9207 AND $0E         ; 0 when the sprite starts on a character row
 $9209 JR Z,$920F      ; two rows of cells only
 $920B ADD HL,DE       ; third row of cells
 $920C LD (HL),C       ;
 $920D INC HL          ;
 $920E LD (HL),C       ;
@label=DrawEntities_Sprite
@isub=LD C,DRAW_COLLIDE
*$920F LD C,$01        ; draw with collision test
 $9211 LD A,(IX+$01)   ;
 $9214 AND (IX+$00)    ;
@isub=OR (IX+ENT_COLUMN)
 $9217 OR (IX+$02)     ;
@isub=AND ENTITY_FRAME_MASK
 $921A AND $E0         ; frame number * 32
 $921C LD E,A          ;
@isub=LD D,(IX+ENT_PAGE)
 $921D LD D,(IX+$05)   ; sprite page
@isub=LD H,RowAddressTable>>8
 $9220 LD H,$82        ;
@isub=LD L,(IX+ENT_Y)
 $9222 LD L,(IX+$03)   ; Y index
@isub=LD A,(IX+ENT_COLUMN)
 $9225 LD A,(IX+$02)   ;
@isub=AND COLUMN_MASK
 $9228 AND $1F         ;
 $922A OR (HL)         ; row address low byte plus column
 $922B INC HL          ;
 $922C LD H,(HL)       ; row address high byte
 $922D LD L,A          ;
 $922E CALL $9456      ; DrawSprite: NZ at the first overlap
 $9231 JP NZ,$90B7     ; overlap: Willy is killed
 $9234 JP $93B3        ; no collision
@label=DrawEntities_Arrow
@isub=BIT ENTITY_DIR_BIT,(IX+$00)
*$9237 BIT 7,(IX+$00)  ; arrow: direction
 $923B JR NZ,$9244     ;
@isub=DEC (IX+ENT_ARROW_X)
 $923D DEC (IX+$04)    ; left: X down by one
@isub=LD C,ARROW_BEEP_LEFT
 $9240 LD C,$2C        ; X value that makes the beep
 $9242 JR $9249        ;
@isub=INC (IX+ENT_ARROW_X)
*$9244 INC (IX+$04)    ; right: X up by one
@isub=LD C,ARROW_BEEP_RIGHT
 $9247 LD C,$F4        ;
@isub=LD A,(IX+ENT_ARROW_X)
*$9249 LD A,(IX+$04)   ;
 $924C CP C            ; beep value reached?
 $924D JR NZ,$9262     ;
@isub=LD BC,2*HI_BYTE+ARROW_BEEP_COUNT
 $924F LD BC,$0280     ; B = 2: first delay; C = 128 toggles
 $9252 LD A,($80DE)    ; border colour of the room
@label=DrawEntities_ArrowBeep
@isub=OUT (ULA_PORT),A
*$9255 OUT ($FE),A     ;
@isub=XOR BEEPER_BITS
 $9257 XOR $18         ;
*$9259 DJNZ $9259      ;
 $925B LD B,C          ; next delay = counter, falling: the pitch rises
 $925C DEC C           ;
 $925D JR NZ,$9255     ;
 $925F JP $93B3        ; the arrow is not drawn in this pass
@label=DrawEntities_ArrowDraw
@isub=AND ~COLUMN_MASK
*$9262 AND $E0         ; X outside 0-31: off screen
 $9264 JP NZ,$93B3     ;
@isub=LD E,(IX+ENT_ARROW_Y)
 $9267 LD E,(IX+$02)   ; Y index of the centre row
@isub=LD D,RowAddressTable>>8
 $926A LD D,$82        ;
 $926C LD A,(DE)       ;
@isub=ADD A,(IX+ENT_ARROW_X)
 $926D ADD A,(IX+$04)  ; plus X
 $9270 LD L,A          ;
 $9271 LD A,E          ; Y index bit 7: upper or lower half of the room
@isub=AND Y_LOWER_HALF
 $9272 AND $80         ;
 $9274 RLCA            ;
@isub=OR SCREEN_ATTRS_BUF>>8
 $9275 OR $5C          ;
 $9277 LD H,A          ; HL = attribute buffer address of the arrow cell
@isub=LD (IX+ENT_ARROW_MASK),0
 $9278 LD (IX+$05),$00 ; collision mask: none
 $927C LD A,(HL)       ;
@isub=AND INK_MASK
 $927D AND $07         ;
@isub=CP WHITE
 $927F CP $07          ; white ink: Willy is in this cell
 $9281 JR NZ,$9286     ;
@isub=DEC (IX+ENT_ARROW_MASK)
 $9283 DEC (IX+$05)    ; mask $FF
*$9286 LD A,(HL)       ;
@isub=OR WHITE
 $9287 OR $07          ; the arrow is white
 $9289 LD (HL),A       ;
 $928A INC DE          ; high byte of the row address
 $928B LD A,(DE)       ;
 $928C LD H,A          ;
 $928D DEC H           ; the pixel row above the centre row
@isub=LD A,(IX+ENT_ARROW_FINS)
 $928E LD A,(IX+$06)   ;
 $9291 LD (HL),A       ; fins
 $9292 INC H           ;
 $9293 LD A,(HL)       ; centre row: anything lit there?
@isub=AND (IX+ENT_ARROW_MASK)
 $9294 AND (IX+$05)    ; only counts in a white-ink cell
 $9297 JP NZ,$90B7     ; Willy is killed
 $929A LD (HL),$FF     ; solid centre row
 $929C INC H           ;
@isub=LD A,(IX+ENT_ARROW_FINS)
 $929D LD A,(IX+$06)   ;
 $92A0 LD (HL),A       ; fins below
 $92A1 JP $93B3        ;
@label=DrawEntities_Rope
*$92A4 LD IY,$8200     ; rope: IY = row table, starts at pixel row 0
@isub=LD (IX+ROPE_SEGMENT),0
 $92A8 LD (IX+$09),$00 ; segment 0 (byte +1 of the next entry)
@isub=LD A,(IX+ENT_COLUMN)
 $92AC LD A,(IX+$02)   ;
@isub=LD (IX+ENT_ROPE_COLUMN),A
 $92AF LD (IX+$03),A   ; current column := column of the top
@isub=LD (IX+ENT_ROPE_MASK),PIXEL_LEFT
 $92B2 LD (IX+$05),$80 ; pixel mask: leftmost pixel
@label=DrawEntities_Segment
*$92B6 LD A,(IY+$00)   ;
@isub=ADD A,(IX+ENT_ROPE_COLUMN)
 $92B9 ADD A,(IX+$03)  ;
 $92BC LD L,A          ; row address low byte plus column
 $92BD LD H,(IY+$01)   ; HL = pixel buffer address of this point
 $92C0 LD A,($85D6)    ; rope variable: 0 = no rope held
 $92C3 OR A            ;
 $92C4 JR NZ,$92D6     ;
@isub=LD A,(IX+ENT_ROPE_MASK)
 $92C6 LD A,(IX+$05)   ; no rope held: is the pixel under this point lit?
 $92C9 AND (HL)        ;
 $92CA JR Z,$930E      ;
@isub=LD A,(IX+ROPE_SEGMENT)
 $92CC LD A,(IX+$09)   ; grab: remember the segment
 $92CF LD ($85D6),A    ;
@isub=SET 0,(IX+ROPE_HELD)
 $92D2 SET 0,(IX+$0B)  ; held flag
@label=DrawEntities_Held
@isub=CP (IX+ROPE_SEGMENT)
*$92D6 CP (IX+$09)     ; is this the segment Willy holds?
 $92D9 JR NZ,$930E     ;
@isub=BIT 0,(IX+ROPE_HELD)
 $92DB BIT 0,(IX+$0B)  ; and does this rope hold him?
 $92DF JR Z,$930E      ;
@isub=LD B,(IX+ENT_ROPE_COLUMN)
 $92E1 LD B,(IX+$03)   ; column
@isub=LD A,(IX+ENT_ROPE_MASK)
 $92E4 LD A,(IX+$05)   ;
 $92E7 LD C,$01        ; from the pixel mask: C = Willy frame, B = column of his left cell
 $92E9 CP $04          ;
 $92EB JR C,$92FC      ;
 $92ED LD C,$00        ;
 $92EF CP $10          ;
 $92F1 JR C,$92FC      ;
 $92F3 DEC B           ;
 $92F4 LD C,$03        ;
 $92F6 CP $40          ;
 $92F8 JR C,$92FC      ;
 $92FA LD C,$02        ;
*$92FC LD ($85D2),BC   ; Willy frame ($85D2) and column ($85D3)
 $9300 LD A,IYl        ; Y index of this point
@isub=SUB Y_ROW_STEP
 $9302 SUB $10         ; minus 8 pixel rows
 $9304 LD ($85CF),A    ; Willy Y index
 $9307 PUSH HL         ;
 $9308 CALL $8E9C      ; Willy attribute address from his Y index and column
 $930B POP HL          ;
 $930C JR $930E        ; (jumps to the next instruction)
@label=DrawEntities_Plot
@isub=LD A,(IX+ENT_ROPE_MASK)
*$930E LD A,(IX+$05)   ; plot the point
 $9311 OR (HL)         ;
 $9312 LD (HL),A       ;
@isub=LD A,(IX+ROPE_SEGMENT)
 $9313 LD A,(IX+$09)   ; segment
 $9316 ADD A,(IX+$01)  ; plus swing position
 $9319 LD L,A          ;
 $931A SET 7,L         ; second half of the rope table
@isub=LD H,RopeStepTable>>8
 $931C LD H,$83        ;
 $931E LD E,(HL)       ; rows down (row table bytes)
 $931F LD D,$00        ;
 $9321 ADD IY,DE       ; IY to the next point
 $9323 RES 7,L         ;
 $9325 LD A,(HL)       ; first half: pixels sideways
 $9326 OR A            ;
 $9327 JR Z,$9350      ;
 $9329 LD B,A          ;
 $932A BIT 7,(IX+$01)  ; side: bit 7 set = left
 $932E JR Z,$9341      ;
@label=DrawEntities_ShiftLeft
@isub=RLC (IX+ENT_ROPE_MASK)
*$9330 RLC (IX+$05)    ; mask one pixel left
@isub=BIT 0,(IX+ENT_ROPE_MASK)
 $9334 BIT 0,(IX+$05)  ; moved into the next byte?
 $9338 JR Z,$933D      ;
@isub=DEC (IX+ENT_ROPE_COLUMN)
 $933A DEC (IX+$03)    ; column left
*$933D DJNZ $9330      ;
 $933F JR $9350        ;
@label=DrawEntities_ShiftRight
@isub=RRC (IX+ENT_ROPE_MASK)
*$9341 RRC (IX+$05)    ; mask one pixel right
@isub=BIT 7,(IX+ENT_ROPE_MASK)
 $9345 BIT 7,(IX+$05)  ; moved into the next byte?
 $9349 JR Z,$934E      ;
@isub=INC (IX+ENT_ROPE_COLUMN)
 $934B INC (IX+$03)    ; column right
*$934E DJNZ $9341      ;
@label=DrawEntities_NextSegment
@isub=LD A,(IX+ROPE_SEGMENT)
*$9350 LD A,(IX+$09)   ; last point?
@isub=CP (IX+ENT_ROPE_LENGTH)
 $9353 CP (IX+$04)     ;
 $9356 JR Z,$935E      ;
@isub=INC (IX+ROPE_SEGMENT)
 $9358 INC (IX+$09)    ;
 $935B JP $92B6        ;
@label=DrawEntities_RopeEnd
*$935E LD A,($85D6)    ; rope variable
 $9361 BIT 7,A         ; $F0-$FF: release countdown
 $9363 JR Z,$936F      ;
 $9365 INC A           ; count up
 $9366 LD ($85D6),A    ;
@isub=RES 0,(IX+ROPE_HELD)
 $9369 RES 0,(IX+$0B)  ; clear the held flag
 $936D JR $93B3        ;
@label=DrawEntities_Climb
@isub=BIT 0,(IX+ROPE_HELD)
*$936F BIT 0,(IX+$0B)  ; rope held?
 $9373 JR Z,$93B3      ;
 $9375 LD A,($85D0)    ; Willy walking state
 $9378 BIT 1,A         ; walking?
 $937A JR Z,$93B3      ;
 $937C RRCA            ; bit 1 of the result: facing left XOR swing direction
 $937D XOR (IX+$00)    ;
 $9380 RLCA            ;
 $9381 RLCA            ;
 $9382 AND $02         ;
 $9384 DEC A           ; +1 or -1
 $9385 LD HL,$85D6     ;
 $9388 ADD A,(HL)      ;
 $9389 LD (HL),A       ; one segment down or up
 $938A LD A,($80EB)    ; up exit of the room
 $938D LD C,A          ;
 $938E LD A,($8420)    ; current room
 $9391 CP C            ; no room above: the up exit is the room itself
 $9392 JR NZ,$939B     ;
 $9394 LD A,(HL)       ;
@isub=CP ROPE_MIN_SEGMENT
 $9395 CP $0C          ;
 $9397 JR NC,$939B     ;
@isub=LD (HL),ROPE_MIN_SEGMENT
 $9399 LD (HL),$0C     ; not higher than this segment
@label=DrawEntities_Limit
*$939B LD A,(HL)       ; past the last segment?
@isub=CP (IX+ENT_ROPE_LENGTH)
 $939C CP (IX+$04)     ;
 $939F JR C,$93B3      ;
 $93A1 JR Z,$93B3      ;
@isub=LD (HL),ROPE_LET_GO
 $93A3 LD (HL),$F0     ; let go at the bottom
 $93A5 LD A,($85CF)    ;
@isub=AND Y_SNAP_MASK
 $93A8 AND $F8         ; Y index down to a multiple of 8
 $93AA LD ($85CF),A    ;
 $93AD XOR A           ;
 $93AE LD ($85D1),A    ; clear the jump/fall state
 $93B1 JR $93B3        ; (jumps to the next instruction)
@label=DrawEntities_Next
@isub=LD DE,ENTITY_SIZE
*$93B3 LD DE,$0008     ;
 $93B6 ADD IX,DE       ;
 $93B8 JP $91C2        ;
